doc:Factspaper1_1 schema1:keywords "Fusion feature space polyhedron" .
_:a64bc609af544395f6667c0972b132af rdf:reifies <<( doc:Factspaper1_1 schema1:keywords "Fusion feature space polyhedron" )>> ;
	prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:6ee264b0e8e8 .
doc:FactsphysicalParameters None:has_text_value "In modern manufacturing, end mill wear monitoring is essential to ensure machining quality and enhance production efficiency. Traditional monitoring methods usually rely on a single source of information; this work proposes multi-source information acquisition and processing based on time windows. Image preprocessing using CLAHE histogram equalization and Sobel operator is applied to extract tool tip wear zones. Sensor signal features are fused using Pearson correlation analysis and polygonal radar charts; a fusion feature space polyhedron fuses multi-source wear information with equal weight and characterizes tool wear by polyhedron volume change. Considering temporal relationships and hyperparameter optimization, an SCSBiLSTMSE neural network predictive model is constructed to predict remaining useful life (RUL) of end mills; model correction via experimental data improves prediction accuracy." .
_:a3b028935d41e6d04835f4eca87cbe4b rdf:reifies <<( doc:FactsphysicalParameters None:has_text_value "In modern manufacturing, end mill wear monitoring is essential to ensure machining quality and enhance production efficiency. Traditional monitoring methods usually rely on a single source of information; this work proposes multi-source information acquisition and processing based on time windows. Image preprocessing using CLAHE histogram equalization and Sobel operator is applied to extract tool tip wear zones. Sensor signal features are fused using Pearson correlation analysis and polygonal radar charts; a fusion feature space polyhedron fuses multi-source wear information with equal weight and characterizes tool wear by polyhedron volume change. Considering temporal relationships and hyperparameter optimization, an SCSBiLSTMSE neural network predictive model is constructed to predict remaining useful life (RUL) of end mills; model correction via experimental data improves prediction accuracy." )>> ;
